    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5492\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize Lord-N-Fields Voice of Freedom Bible Church Community\nWorkers International Inc. to file an application for exemption from\nreal property taxes for a certain parcel of land located in the town of\nBrookhaven, county of Suffolk\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo grant the village assessor for the town of Brookhaven the authority\nto exempt Lord-N-Fields Voice of Freedom Bible Church Community\nWorkers International Inc., a not-for-profit organization, from\nliability for payment of real property taxes due on the\n2008-2009,2009-2010 and 2010-2011 assessment rolls.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection One authorizes and directs the assessor of the town of\nBrookhaven to accept an application from the Lord-N-Fields Voice of\nFreedom Bible Church Community Workers International Inc. for\nexemption from real property taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the\nreal property tax law for the assessment rolls as completed in\n2008-2009, 2009-2010 and 2010-2011 for their property located in\nBrookhaven. Upon satisfaction that this organization would have\notherwise been entitled to said exemption, the assessor may grant\nthis exemption from all taxation beginning with respect to this roll.\nIf exemption is granted, the organization may be refunded any taxes\npaid and any taxes, fines, penalties, liens or interest unpaid may be\ncancelled through the sole discretion of the Brookhaven Town Board.\nSection Two is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nLord-N-Fields Voice of Freedom Bible Church Community Workers\nInternational Inc.\npurchased their property at 82-84 Beaverdam Road, town of Brookhaven,\nSuffolk County, New York, for the purpose of building a new church\nhowever they were not able to apply for and be granted tax exempt\nstatus at that time. This bill would authorize the assessor of the\ntown of Brookhaven to accept application from this organization for\nexemption from real property taxes pursuant to Section 420-a of the\nreal property tax law for the 2008-2009, 2009-2010 and 20102011\nassessment rolls.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
